# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the tests (TRAVERSO_TSAN builds; ctest
# passes this file in TSAN_OPTIONS, tests/CMakeLists.txt).
#
# Only reports whose racing accesses are inside Qt or glib, which are not
# instrumented: they synchronise with their own locks and atomics, which TSan
# cannot see. Each pattern is a Qt or glib function that is never on a
# Traverso stack except as Qt's own callee. Checked 2026-10-31 with a probe
# (two QThreads racing on an int in our own code): still reported with this
# file. The analysis with the stacks: reports/tsan-clean-2026-10-31 (local).
# Needs Qt's debug information (Qt 6.12.0 "Debug Information Files" with the
# matching Qt build), else the Qt frames have no names and nothing matches.

# Qt: a QObject's binding status, made when a QThread starts (on the starting
# thread) and freed or cleared on that QThread; QThreadData's own clean-up.
# Reached from TAudioThreadMessageQueue::make_instance() and the end of
# TAudioDeviceThread::run() (its WatchDogThread).
race:QtPrivate::BindingStatusOrList
race:initBindingStatus

# Qt: QThreadPool's task queue, allocated in enqueueTask() and freed by the
# pool thread that runs the task.
race:QThreadPoolPrivate::enqueueTask

# Qt: QThreadPool's list of its threads.
race:QArrayDataPointer<QThreadPoolThread*>

# glib: a GRWLock initialised lazily with glib's own atomics (Qt's event
# dispatcher on pool threads).
race:g_rw_lock_reader_lock

# Traverso: the hand-over of a step to QThreadPool (s_handOverFence in
# TIOScheduler.h). The step lambda reads what QRunnable::create() copied on
# the scheduler thread. TSan ziet de lock van QThreadPool niet; verdwijnt bij
# T71 stap 2c (eigen pools). race_top: only an access in the lambda's own
# body, not in the stream's step() it calls. Remove with T71 step 2c
# (doc/status.md).
race_top:TIOScheduler::start_stream_step
race_top:TIOScheduler::start_task_step
